.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Vt struct mbt_storage
is a reference-counted object that holds torrent data.
Sessions and torrents take their own references, so the caller can drop its
reference after it passes the storage to a session or torrent.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_storage_new
makes a storage with one reference from a
.Vt struct mbt_storage_ops
and a context pointer.
It returns
.Dv NULL
if it cannot allocate memory.
.Fn mbt_storage_ref
adds a reference.
.Fn mbt_storage_unref
removes one, and calls the
.Fa destroy
operation when the last reference goes.
Both accept
.Dv NULL .
.Sh BACKEND OPERATIONS
.Fa open
receives the context and a torrent, and sets its last argument to a
.Vt struct mbt_storage_handle
that is not
.Dv NULL .
The torrent passes this handle to
.Fa write_piece ,
.Fa read_piece ,
.Fa have_piece
and
.Fa close .
The torrent calls
.Fa close
before it drops its reference to the storage.
.Fa destroy
is optional.
.Pp
.Fa remove ,
.Fa exists ,
.Fa sync
and
.Fa mark
are optional.
.Xr mbt_torrent_move_storage 3
needs
.Fa remove
on both storages, and uses the others on the target.
.Pp
.Fa remove
deletes the data of an open torrent.
The handle stays valid for
.Fa close .
.Pp
.Fa exists
returns 1 if data for the torrent blocks a move, and 0 if not.
.Pp
.Fa sync
returns after all writes are durable.
.Pp
.Fa mark
records that a move into the storage has started, or clears that record when
.Fa on
is 0.
.Fa exists
ignores data that a mark covers, so a move can retry after a crash.
File storage uses a file named
.Pa .mbt-move-<infohash>
in the data directory.
.Pp
.Fa read_only
returns 1 if the storage takes no writes.
The torrent then requests no pieces, and logs the pieces that fail its verify.
.Sh FILE STORAGE
.Fn mbt_storage_file_new
makes a storage for files under
.Fa data_dir .
It holds any number of torrents.
A single-file torrent uses
.Pa data_dir/name .
A multi-file torrent uses
.Pa data_dir/torrent_name/path .
.Fa open
fails with
.Er EEXIST
if a file path is in use by a torrent that is open on this storage.
.Sh DESCRIPTOR STORAGE
.Fn mbt_storage_fd_new
makes a storage for one single-file torrent on an open descriptor.
It calls no path API, so it works in a sandbox with no file access.
.Fa fd
must be a regular file without
.Dv O_APPEND ,
open for read and write.
With
.Dv MBT_STORAGE_FD_READONLY
it can be open for read only, its size must equal the torrent size, and the
torrent only seeds.
.Pp
On success the storage owns
.Fa fd ,
and the last reference closes it.
If the function returns
.Dv NULL ,
the caller still owns
.Fa fd .
A second
.Fa open
fails with
.Er EBUSY .
.Fa open
fails with
.Er EINVAL
for a multi-file torrent, a file that is not regular, a file with
.Dv O_APPEND ,
or a file of the wrong size.
The storage does not call
.Xr fsync 2 .
.Sh MEMORY STORAGE
The memory backend holds one torrent at a time in a flat buffer.
A second
.Fa open
fails with
.Er EBUSY .
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_new
makes a memory storage.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_destroy
drops the reference that
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_new
made.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_storage
returns the storage and adds no reference.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_put_file
writes into the buffer at an offset, and grows the buffer if necessary.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_get_file
reads from the buffer at an offset.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_data
returns the buffer.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_length
returns the size of the buffer.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt 3 ,
